  "response": "# Merge triage for `02-react-dashboard`, petty / single-file findings\n\nI categorised from the scan JSON you supplied and did not run `crimes scan` again. The scan has 83 findings: 0 high, 54 medium, 29 low.\n\n**Scope.** You asked about petty / single-file findings. 36 of the 83 fit that. The other 47 are cross-file duplication: 46 `exact_duplicate_block` and 1 `duplicate_component_shape`. I've left those out, with a short note at the end.\n\n**Rule applied.** Every finding below was sorted by these thresholds:\n\n| Category | Criteria |\n|---|---|\n| **Block merge** | severity ≥ medium (0.5+) **and** `agent_risk` ≥ 0.35 |\n| **Warn** | medium severity with `agent_risk` < 0.35, **or** low severity with `agent_risk` ≥ 0.30 |\n| **Ignore** | low severity with `agent_risk` < 0.30, including all asset findings (`agent_risk` ≤ 0.07) |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Repeated role/status checks: `duplicated_role_status_plan_check`\n\n| ID | Literal | Sev (score) | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crime_00002 | `\"paid\"` | medium (0.55) | **0.36** | 🛑 **Block** |\n| crime_00003 | `\"pending\"` | medium (0.55) | **0.36** | 🛑 **Block** |\n\n- **Why block:** these are the second-highest `agent_risk` scores in the scan, and they carry the highest severity among in-scope findings. Each status is compared in 4 files using 2 expression shapes (`invoice.status === \"paid\"` vs `status === \"paid\"`), in `edit-form.tsx` and `status.tsx` in both the starter and final apps. A new status, or a renamed one, would have to change in every one of those places, and the 2 shapes make it easy to miss one.\n- **Fix before merge:** add one `isPaid` / `isPending` helper, or an `InvoiceStatus` const, and call it from both `status.tsx` and `edit-form.tsx`. Effort: medium.\n\n## 2. Magic literals: `magic_domain_literal_scatter`\n\n| ID | Literal | Sev (score) | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crime_00001 | `\"status\"` | medium (0.5) | **0.41** | 🛑 **Block** (ver