ch suggests they are deliberate \"uncomment this in chapter N\" scaffolding. If so, ask for a one-line comment saying so. If not, delete them (effort: quick).\n- **Ignore:** the 2–8 line snippets at 0.29 are commented-out debug lines (`console.log('Fetching revenue data...')`, a fake delay) and similar small leftovers. They are below the threshold and cost little.\n\n## 4. Other single-file detectors\n\n| Detector | IDs | Sev (score) | agent_risk | Verdict | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `direct_date` | crime_00061 (`actions.ts:57`) | low (0.35) | 0.28 | ✅ Ignore | The scan says the date is only recorded, never used in a branch. That is the normal pattern for a server action stamping a date. |\n| `singular_plural_type_mismatch` | crime_00062, 00063 (`revenue: Revenue[]`) | low (0.30) | 0.28 | ✅ Ignore | \"Revenue\" is a mass noun, so this is a detector false positive. Add `revenue` to `allowedNames`. |\n| `deep_import` | crime_00064, 00065 (`react-syntax-highlighter/dist/cjs/styles/prism`) | low (0.35) | 0.07 | ✅ Ignore | This is the import path the library documents for its styles. |\n| `raster_should_be_vector` | crime_00066 – 00077 (12 customer avatars, 56–60 px) | low (0.35) | 0.05 | ✅ Ignore | These are photos, not icons, so SVG doesn't apply. |\n| `oversized_raster` | crime_00078 – 00083 (237–487 KB) | low (0.40) | 0.04 | ✅ Ignore | Lowest `agent_risk` in the scan. `hero-desktop.png` (486.6 KB) is close to the 500 KB medium line. Consider WebP in a later PR. |\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| Category | Count | IDs |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🛑 Block merge | **3** | 00001, 00002, 00003 (all part of the same status-policy problem; one fix covers all three) |\n| ⚠️ Warn | **6** | 00004–00008, 00017 |\n| ✅ Ignore | **27** | 00018–00021, 00061–00083 |\n\n**Cross-file findings (out of scope).** The 47 duplication findings score `agent_risk` 0.28–0.31 at medium severity. Under the same rule they would all be **warn**, none block. Nearly all of them are copies between `starter-example` and `final-example`, or between the `basics/*` tutorial steps. In a tutorial repo that duplication is the point, so I would ignore them, or exclude those directories from the scan.\n\n**Overall:** request changes on one item, the invoice-status policy (paid/pending checks plus the `status` field literal). Everything else is advisory or noise.",
